A private social network for your family, on a device you own
Off The Cloud is free, open-source software that gives your family a social network of its own. You post photos and videos, comment and like, and only the friends you accept see them. Each family keeps its posts on its own small device at home, a Raspberry Pi 5, and friends' devices share them with each other, so no company holds your photos, shows you ads or decides what you see. The same device backs up your phones and keeps your files.
@a.href=https://demo.off-the.cloud/
Try the demo Look around a real device with a made-up family's photos and files. No sign-up.
What your family gets
A feed of the people you know. Photos and videos, several to a post, with a caption, comments and likes, newest first. Nothing suggested and nothing sponsored.
Notifications that matter. Your phone tells you when someone accepts your friend request, likes or comments: nothing designed to keep you scrolling.
Room for the whole family. Give each person an account on your device, with their own address, photo library and password, and be friends with each other in the feed.
You decide what stays. Delete a post or a comment and it goes from your friends' devices too. Remove a friend and you can delete everything they shared with you, and ask their device to delete what you shared there.
Links for everyone else. Send a collection to the grandparents as a link that expires: they open it in their browser, with no account or app, and can download the originals.
Your photos, already safe. The same device backs up every phone in the family in full resolution and keeps your files, so what you post is already backed up at home.
What's different from the big apps
Nobody in between. Your posts are on your device, and your friends' devices fetch them from it. Our bridge relays the connection and keeps none of what passes through, so there's no company server holding everyone's photos.
No ads, no algorithm, no AI training. Nothing is sold, nothing ranks your feed, and nothing you post is used to train AI models.
Everyone has an account on a device. Each person in the feed has an account on an Off The Cloud device, their own or yours, with an off-the.cloud address. The bridge account that gives the addresses is free for two years, then €9.99 + VAT a year.
No private messages, on purpose. With no chats or direct messages, there's less room for bullying or for a stranger to approach a child: what people share is posts and comments, and only with the friends they accept.
