FAQ
Questions people actually ask
Can my friends see my photo library?
No. Friends see only what you post in the feed. Your photo library, your files and the other accounts on your device stay private: a friend's device can only fetch the photos and videos of your posts.
Why are there no private messages?
On purpose, to make the network safer, for children above all. Without chats or direct messages, there's less room for bullying or for a stranger to approach a child: what people share is posts and comments, and only the friends someone accepts see their posts or can comment on them. Nobody can be found by searching, either: there's no directory and no suggested friends, so a friend request needs the exact address.
Does it work with Mastodon, Pixelfed or the fediverse?
No. Off The Cloud devices only talk to each other: your posts never appear on the fediverse, and you can't follow fediverse accounts from it. That's part of what keeps it private: your posts are never public, and there's no search for strangers to find you with.
What does it cost?
The software is free and open source. You need a Raspberry Pi 5 and two USB drives, bought once, and an off-the.cloud address for everyone in the feed: the bridge account is free for its first two years, then €9.99 + VAT a year with up to five addresses, and the accounts you add for your family on your device don't count toward those five.
